<groundspeak:short_description html="False"><![CDATA[
Vloženo : 2026-09-21
Drive in : NE
Ověřeno: Na výchozích
Poznámky :
At what depth do the bubbles appear? From 1.5 m
Q2: What is the seabed made of? (Rocks, pebbles, or sand) Sand
Q3: Do the bubbles always emerge from the same spots, or do these locations change? Why do you think that is?
They change; the sand allows new paths for the gas to form. Q4: How many water molecules and how many carbon dioxide molecules are needed to form one molecule of carbonic acid? One molecule of water ([H₂O]) and one molecule of carbon dioxide ([CO₂]) are needed to form one molecule of carbonic acid.
]]></groundspeak:short_description>
